  "summary_en": "European Commission 2012 legislative proposal to replace Directive 98/79/EC with a Regulation on in vitro diagnostic medical devices, introducing a four-class risk classification, stronger notified-body oversight, UDI traceability, Eudamed registration, clinical evidence rules and an EU vigilance portal. Not about AI or robotics; later adopted as Regulation (EU) 2017/746.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Introduces risk-based classification of IVDs into classes A-D with proportionate conformity assessment",
   "Strengthens designation and monitoring of notified bodies, including joint assessments and unannounced inspections",
   "Requires Unique Device Identification and central registration in Eudamed",
   "Sets clinical evidence and clinical performance study requirements with ethics and consent safeguards",
   "Creates EU vigilance portal for serious incident reporting and coordination via the MDCG"
  ],
